1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,552
Welcome to Mutable Dreams.

2
00:00:03,552 --> 00:00:10,538
A six voice instrument for the M Vave F M one, and a
playable instrument in your browser.

3
00:00:10,538 --> 00:00:15,582
Its roots are in the generous work of Émilie Gillet
and Mutable Instruments.

4
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:21,404
Selected Plaits voices and a Rings resonator meet
our own choir, rhythms, and granular cloud.

5
00:00:21,404 --> 00:00:23,732
Let us begin with a Biome.

6
00:00:24,732 --> 00:00:27,289
Start the instrument, then press Play.

7
00:00:27,289 --> 00:00:33,680
The Atlas holds sixty four musical Biomes, from soft
atmospheres to dub, percussion, and melody.

8
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,663
Search by name or choose a landscape.

9
00:00:36,663 --> 00:00:38,793
Each Biome is completely editable.

10
00:00:38,793 --> 00:00:44,332
Blank Biome clears the patterns and cloud, leaving
space for your own composition.

11
00:00:44,332 --> 00:00:47,315
Save your work before choosing another world.

12
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:51,045
Select any of the six tracks.

13
00:00:51,045 --> 00:00:55,139
Choose a sound preset, or choose its engine
directly.

14
00:00:55,139 --> 00:00:59,688
There are one hundred and twenty eight sounds to
explore.

15
00:00:59,688 --> 00:01:08,786
Every track can be a kick, snare, hi hat, F M voice,
virtual analogue oscillator, resonator, harmonic
voice, or choir.

16
00:01:08,786 --> 00:01:12,881
Sound presets preserve your rhythm, notes, level,
and send.

17
00:01:12,881 --> 00:01:17,885
The keyboard plays the selected voice; octave
buttons move its range.

18
00:01:18,885 --> 00:01:22,000
Home brings you to the live controls.

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,225
Density adds or removes events.

20
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:26,006
Motion varies melodic notes.

21
00:01:26,006 --> 00:01:28,231
Colour moves brightness and overtones.

22
00:01:28,231 --> 00:01:30,901
Space brings the granular cloud forward.

23
00:01:30,901 --> 00:01:34,906
Start with small movements, and let the pattern
breathe.

24
00:01:34,906 --> 00:01:45,142
On the instrument, Select chooses a track, Algo
chooses its engine, and Preset chooses a Biome from
Home, or a sound from Edit.

25
00:01:46,142 --> 00:01:49,483
Sequence opens hits, length, rotation, and chance.

26
00:01:49,483 --> 00:01:55,209
Tap it again for swing, repeats, accents, and each
track's clock division.

27
00:01:55,209 --> 00:01:59,981
These let a simple pulse become a slowly shifting
conversation.

28
00:01:59,981 --> 00:02:03,798
Global opens harmony: root, scale, transpose, and
tempo.

29
00:02:03,798 --> 00:02:07,139
Eight shared scales keep melodic voices together.

30
00:02:07,139 --> 00:02:14,297
Arp locks the seed, Record creates a variation, and
Envelope returns to the previous variation.

31
00:02:15,297 --> 00:02:18,534
Edit cycles through sound, filter, envelope, and
mix.

32
00:02:18,534 --> 00:02:25,818
Shape your tone and harmonics, soften it with a low
pass filter, or try the low pass gate.

33
00:02:25,818 --> 00:02:27,842
Breathe adds slow filter movement.

34
00:02:27,842 --> 00:02:31,889
Melodic voices offer a gentle attack and a long
decay.

35
00:02:31,889 --> 00:02:36,340
Mix sets the grain send, base note, pan, and clock
division.

36
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:38,768
Select's button mutes the selected track.

37
00:02:39,768 --> 00:02:41,854
Effects opens the granular bus.

38
00:02:41,854 --> 00:02:43,523
Space sets its level.

39
00:02:43,523 --> 00:02:49,364
Grain size shapes the fragments; position explores
the sound memory; feedback lets them linger.

40
00:02:49,364 --> 00:02:51,033
Larger grains overlap smoothly.

41
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:59,378
Tap Effects again to transpose or reverse the tape,
and choose a track to duck the other voices and
cloud.

42
00:02:59,378 --> 00:03:02,298
L F O freezes the recorded material.

43
00:03:02,298 --> 00:03:05,219
Listen as the rhythm continues around it.

44
00:03:06,219 --> 00:03:09,642
Hold any function button for its help page.

45
00:03:09,642 --> 00:03:13,494
Release it, then tap once to close the page.

46
00:03:13,494 --> 00:03:16,490
Global also leads to System and Look.

47
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:20,770
Choose Eco or Full quality; heavier combinations
automatically use Eco.

48
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:24,622
Reset the CPU peak when measuring a new patch.

49
00:03:24,622 --> 00:03:29,329
Look controls animation, the optional startup sound,
and replaying the introduction.

50
00:03:30,329 --> 00:03:34,795
Stop playback and press Save to keep your patch and
preferences.

51
00:03:34,795 --> 00:03:37,230
There is one personal patch slot.

52
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:41,696
Factory Biomes remain available, and browser saves
stay in that browser.

53
00:03:41,696 --> 00:03:48,191
Panic stops playback and clears the cloud; on the F
M one, use Record from System.

54
00:03:48,191 --> 00:03:53,062
Begin quietly, take your time, and make these small
worlds your own.

55
00:03:53,062 --> 00:03:55,092
With gratitude to Mutable Instruments.
